### Exact-tree tests

The complete base importer/package set was run from the clean refreshed-trunk
archive (`.temp/TASK-260830-2h5uv9/importer/base-origin-main`) with
`go test ./... -v -count=1`: exit 0, 45/45 package summaries green. Raw output is
`.temp/TASK-260830-2h5uv9/importer/base-origin-main-full.log`. The exact
candidate tree ran `go test ./... -v -skip
'^TestDurableSyncGeneratedPerturbationProduct$' -count=1`: exit 0, 46/46
package summaries green, recorded at
`.temp/TASK-260830-2h5uv9/full-configured-suite-final-01.log`. The single
generated property test is run separately because its full product exceeds a
bounded shell call; all 38,000 scenarios passed across the 46 accepted
single-process shards listed in
`.temp/TASK-260830-2h5uv9/generated-property-shards.md`. Thus the base and
candidate importer package sets were each executed, and every candidate test
including the generated product is covered by a green accepted run.

No pre-existing direct-import edge moved between the refreshed base and this
candidate; the only graph additions are the 46 edges from the new
`internal/merkleinventory` package, listed above. The observable moved classes
are: Section 10.7 Tombstone and Tombstone Acknowledgement identity inputs move
from fail-closed to admitted after their exact shape, coupling, and digest
checks; unsupported mapped schemas remain fail-closed; durable sync adds
monotone immutable union, delayed-gap recovery, quarantine/abort on same-ID
byte conflict, and repository-bound projection; validated lease tuple reads
do not select winners by timestamp; and the traceability registry gains the
three Story leaf cases and its re-derived digest. The importer outcome grid
above maps each changed package entry and input class to its named executed
tests; all other package paths and importer outcomes are unchanged in the
base/candidate package runs.

